    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/mansourvery-hub/anki-japanese-template/commit/fb0f27fca45b7694a304b531a0703f49692d8bd9"/>
    <title>
        test_layout: font-independent overflow guarantee (CI has no CJK fonts)
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-11T23:50:47Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/f8fe6ac7d7180ce9a550fcd981d25751?d=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.githubassets.com%2Fimages%2Fgravatars%2Fgravatar-user-420.png&amp;r=g&amp;s=30"/>
    <author>
      <name></name>
      <email>mohamed@example.com</email>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;test_layout: font-independent overflow guarantee (CI has no CJK fonts)

CI runners have Chrome but no CJK fonts, so the Japanese definition
fixture rendered with fallback tofu metrics and fit inside the 3-line
cap — the truncator never fired. A fixed-height spacer inside the
definition box makes scrollHeight &amp;gt; clientHeight true in every
environment, so the truncator checks no longer depend on fonts.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/75d9e9b08a6f2ba0a314da7b34b8db76a437e928</id>
    <link type="text/html" rel="alternate" href="https://github.com/mansourvery-hub/anki-japanese-template/commit/75d9e9b08a6f2ba0a314da7b34b8db76a437e928"/>
    <title>
        Minimal redesign: pure retrieval front, quiet hierarchical back
    </title>
    <updated>2026-09-11T23:02:39Z</updated>
    <media:thumbnail height="30" width="30" url="https://1.gravatar.com/avatar/f8fe6ac7d7180ce9a550fcd981d25751?d=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.githubassets.com%2Fimages%2Fgravatars%2Fgravatar-user-420.png&amp;r=g&amp;s=30"/>
    <author>
      <name></name>
      <email>mohamed@example.com</email>
    </author>
    <content type="html">
      &lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Minimal redesign: pure retrieval front, quiet hierarchical back

Front: hidden behavioral probes; listening resolver (classic audio-only
fields OR #listening tag) with the sentence front as universal fallback;
no note: search clause ({{Type}} is scheduling type, not model).

Back: word -&amp;gt; pitch -&amp;gt; meaning -&amp;gt; context-grid (sentence+picture)
hierarchy; secondary info collapsed behind More; discreet Context/Word/
Listening state label; F full-card furigana, T translation reveal.
Tags bar + frequency/pitch badges removed (tags = behavioral metadata).

Also: JS syntax gate in tests (unbalanced-brace regression caught by QA),
mobile word-meta-row specificity fix, stale 6c comment, unused import,
front-modes behavioral test suite.&lt;/pre&gt;
    </content>
  </entry>
